# A gate is driven by a real `spec-test` sub-run, so the runner makes its usual scratch here:
# `.spec-tmp/` (already ignored repo-wide) and a `fragments/<target>/` tree.
#
# ⚠⚠ **THIS LINE IS NOW LOAD-BEARING, AND UNTIL 2026-08-23 IT WAS ONLY INSURANCE.** The orphaned-golden
# gate (`HarnessSelfTest.requireOrphanedGoldensAreReported`) WRITES `.test` files under
# `orphan-golden/fragments/x64-windows/` on every suite run — deliberately, because the census it proves
# can only be shown to fire against a golden nothing declares — and removes them again before it
# returns. They are planted rather than committed so the gate also gets its NEGATIVE control: the same
# fixture is run a second time with them gone, and the census must then say nothing. An interrupted run
# leaves one behind, and this line is what keeps that from becoming a tracked file.
#
# The other reason it was here still holds. The live-network gate's case is deliberately made to FAIL
# (its pinned stdout is wrong on purpose — see `requireNetworkGateHolds`, which asserts on the FAIL
# verdict line), and a case that fails never reaches the golden write, so that fixture mints nothing.
# The orphan gate's active case is deliberately made to fail for exactly that reason too. Correct either
# stdout, or add a gate whose case passes, and every `spec-test` in this checkout starts minting `.test`
# goldens here — which nothing reads back and no gate asserts on.
fragments/
